      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Introducing an artificial discontinuity at $r = 0.5 R_{moon}$ to match the seismic decay will artificially inflate the resonant frequencies and damp the modes, potentially masking the \"residuals\" you perceive as validation for your hollow hypothesis. While mathematically you can force a fit by assuming infinite shear modulus contrast, such a model would be physically unstable and inconsistent with the Moon's thermal history and magnetic stray field data which suggest a liquid outer core rather than a manufactured shell. The lack of convergence in real science is usually due to the complex, distributed nature of the damping mechanisms in the lithosphere, not because standard equations fail to account for a non-geological artifact.",
